   "text": "The model wrote a `redlock` decorator by typing it into `/tmp/decorator.py` with a heredoc [T0B23:<RANGE>cat > /tmp/decorator.py <<'EOF'</RANGE>]. It then spliced that into `pottery/redlock.py` [T0B25]. Its functional checks passed [T0B46:<RANGE>Critical section\nlock exists after: 0</RANGE>]. The two `test_redlock` failures were also present before the change [T0B72:<RANGE>FAILED (failures=2)</RANGE>].\n\nNext it ran `git diff` with no pager guard [T0B73:<RANGE>cd /testbed && git diff</RANGE>]. That dropped the terminal into `less` [T0B76:<RANGE>Pattern not found  (press RETURN)</RANGE>]. Every later command was typed into the pager. Typing `echo ok` into `less` opened its help screen [T0B94:<RANGE>HELP -- Press RETURN for more, or q when done</RANGE>]. One `q` briefly worked [T0B95:<RANGE>bash_command(keystrokes=q</RANGE>]. After that the model sent `echo ok` again about 38 times without changing approach, and the help screen never cleared [T0B171:<RANGE>bash_command(keystrokes=echo ok</RANGE>].\n\nThe model never added the planned test and never sent task_complete. The run ended with TrialBudgetExhaustedError after 87 episodes and reward 0. That is fewer than the ~120-call request ceiling, and each repeated turn carried a large help-screen observation, which points to the input-token budget running out.",
